WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.280
In fall, a snowshoe hare's brown fur turns white over several weeks.

2
00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:13.160
On snow, the white hare is hard to see.

3
00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:17.880
But what if the snow melts early, and the hare is still white?

4
00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:19.900
What happens to this hare?

5
00:00:20.633 --> 00:00:23.453
An adaptation is an inherited trait.

6
00:00:24.153 --> 00:00:28.833
It helps a living thing survive and reproduce, which means have young.

7
00:00:30.173 --> 00:00:33.733
Inherited means the trait passes from parents to their young.

8
00:00:34.693 --> 00:00:37.133
A hare's white coat is one adaptation.

9
00:00:38.067 --> 00:00:41.367
A physical adaptation is a feature of the body.

10
00:00:42.107 --> 00:00:45.707
It can be a body covering, a color, or a structure.

11
00:00:46.907 --> 00:00:49.067
A heron's long legs are a structure.

12
00:00:50.247 --> 00:00:52.727
A behavioral adaptation is an action.

13
00:00:54.147 --> 00:00:57.867
Migration is a regular journey between places used in different seasons.

14
00:00:59.107 --> 00:01:01.427
Monarch butterflies fly south in fall.

15
00:01:02.217 --> 00:01:04.797
The hare's white coat is camouflage.

16
00:01:05.917 --> 00:01:09.957
Camouflage is coloring that helps an animal blend in with its background.

17
00:01:10.997 --> 00:01:13.937
On snow, the white coat helps hide the hare.

18
00:01:14.677 --> 00:01:16.497
It does not make the hare invisible.

19
00:01:17.537 --> 00:01:20.837
On bare brown ground, the same coat stands out.

20
00:01:21.637 --> 00:01:22.757
That is a trade-off.

21
00:01:23.637 --> 00:01:28.057
A trade-off means a trait helps in one way but costs in another.

22
00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:32.010
Hares in one forest are not all alike.

23
00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:36.350
In Montana, some hares turned white earlier than others.

24
00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:40.650
These differences between individuals are called variation.

25
00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:44.630
A single hare cannot decide to change color.

26
00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:50.470
Change happens to a population, all the members of one species in one area.

27
00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:56.190
Hares whose inherited timing fits the snow may survive and have more young.

28
00:01:56.190 --> 00:02:00.370
Over many generations, that timing can become more common.

29
00:02:01.283 --> 00:02:05.163
So what happens to a white hare when the snow melts early?

30
00:02:05.883 --> 00:02:08.263
It stands out on bare brown ground.

31
00:02:08.943 --> 00:02:10.743
Predators can spot it more easily.

32
00:02:11.523 --> 00:02:14.023
A single hare cannot choose a new coat.

33
00:02:14.643 --> 00:02:17.683
Only populations change, over many generations.
